Perfect. Since you're learning the full end-to-end process, I would recommend starting clean and recreating everything using the Azure Portal and GitHub Actions OIDC.



Current Project Structure



Based on what you've shared, you'll need something like:



nodejs-demo/

│

├── app.js

├── package.json

├── Dockerfile

├── .dockerignore

└── .github

    └── workflows

        └── docker-build.yml



Your app.js looks fine and will work as-is.



Phase 1 - Create Azure Container Registry (Portal)



In the Azure Portal:



Create Resource

    └── Container Registry



Fill in:



Subscription:

<your subscription>



Resource Group:

rg-nodejs-demo



Registry Name:

ansujacr001



The registry name must be globally unique.



SKU:

Basic



Click:



Review + Create



After deployment completes:



Container Registries

   └── ansujacr001



Copy:



Login Server



ansujacr001.azurecr.io

Phase 2 - Create Azure Container App Environment



Create:



Container App Environment



Example:



Name:

nodejs-env



Region:

UK South



Resource Group:

rg-nodejs-demo

Phase 3 - Create Azure Container App



Create:



Container App



For now you can use any temporary image from ACR.



Example:



Name:

nodejs-app



Container App Environment:

nodejs-env



Ingress:

External



Target Port:

3000



We'll update the image automatically from GitHub Actions later.



Phase 4 - Configure GitHub Secrets



Repository:



Settings

   └── Secrets and Variables

          └── Actions



Create:



AZURE_CLIENT_ID

AZURE_TENANT_ID

AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID

ACR_NAME

RESOURCE_GROUP

CONTAINER_APP_NAME



Example:



AZURE_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxx

AZURE_TENANT_ID=xxxxxxxx

AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=xxxxxxxx



ACR_NAME=ansujacr001



RESOURCE_GROUP=rg-nodejs-demo



CONTAINER_APP_NAME=nodejs-app

Phase 5 - GitHub Actions Pipeline



Create:



.github/workflows/docker-build.yml



Paste:



name: Build and Deploy NodeJS



on:

  push:

    branches:

      - main



permissions:

  id-token: write

  contents: read



env:

  IMAGE_NAME: nodejs-demo



jobs:

  build:



    runs-on: ubuntu-latest



    steps:



      - name: Checkout Source

        uses: actions/checkout@v4



      - name: Azure Login (OIDC)

        uses: azure/login@v2

        with:

          client-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_CLIENT_ID }}

          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_TENANT_ID }}

          subscription-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID }}



      - name: Login to Azure Container Registry

        run: |

          az acr login --name ${{ secrets.ACR_NAME }}



      - name: Build Docker Image

        run: |

          docker build \

          -t ${{ secrets.ACR_NAME }}.azurecr.io/${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}:${{ github.run_number }} \

          -t ${{ secrets.ACR_NAME }}.azurecr.io/${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}:latest .



      - name: Push Docker Image

        run: |

          docker push ${{ secrets.ACR_NAME }}.azurecr.io/${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}:${{ github.run_number }}

          docker push ${{ secrets.ACR_NAME }}.azurecr.io/${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}:latest



      - name: Update Azure Container App

        run: |

          az containerapp update \

            --name ${{ secrets.CONTAINER_APP_NAME }} \

            --resource-group ${{ secrets.RESOURCE_GROUP }} \

            --image ${{ secrets.ACR_NAME }}.azurecr.io/${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}:latest

Phase 6 - Commit Everything

git add .

git commit -m "Add GitHub Actions OIDC pipeline"

git push origin main

