Application Available

One More File You'll Need



I don't see a package.json in the files you've listed. Your Docker build will fail without it because your Node.js app depends on Express.



Create a package.json like this:



{

  "name": "nodejs-demo",

  "version": "1.0.0",

  "main": "app.js",

  "scripts": {

    "start": "node app.js"

  },

  "dependencies": {

    "express": "^4.21.2"

  }

}



Then run:



npm install



which creates:



package-lock.json



Commit both files before running the GitHub Actions pipeline. Otherwise the Docker image build will fail during dependency installation.



